 {'id':'IR01-SCOPE-014','severity':'required_scope_restoration','question_id':'Q014','exact_question':question['Q014'],'exact_question_phrase':'how does Standing change, and when are expectations and dividends checked?','source_truth':'Immediate failure during Revenue goes directly to Final Scoring.','asked_scope':'Required consequential stopping exception to the expressly requested check/dividend timing.','exact_before':'Reaching failure ends game immediately [removed from mandatory facts by FB-Q014-09]','exact_after':'If an emergency-loan/expectations Standing reduction reaches the failure space, go to Final Scoring immediately; do not proceed with remaining Revenue steps. Otherwise check expectations after expenses/Public Embarrassment, then consider dividends.','proposed_change':'Restore the removed Q014 failure atom; qualify subsequent timing atoms with survival. The key already contains the failure rule, so preserve it.','evidence':[ev(1900,1902,27),ev(1918,1934,27)],'reason':'The question asks when later checks happen in a shortfall procedure. A loss of Standing can end that procedure before the later steps. Treating this as merely adjacent endgame context would allow an answer that wrongly continues to expectations or dividends after failure. Coverage elsewhere does not make a condition unasked here.','coverage_consequence':'No new question needed for this condition; retain it under Q014 even though Q025 also tests game end.'},
 {'id':'IR01-SCOPE-025','severity':'unasked_mandatory_context','question_id':'Q025','atom_index_1_based':8,'exact_question':question['Q025'],'exact_question_phrase':'Can promises or negotiations continue in Final Scoring?','source_truth':'The explicit-card exception in this paragraph qualifies playing blackmail; it does not provide a general exception to the ban on negotiations or cashing promises.','asked_scope':'Blackmail permission is not requested by this question.','exact_before':'Explicit card permissions can override','exact_after':None,'proposed_change':'Move Q025 atom 8 to optional blackmail context, explicitly limited to playing blackmail cards. Keep Q025 atoms 1–7 mandatory.','evidence':[ev(843,847,9)],'reason':'The two requested final-scoring activities are promises and negotiations. A complete answer can prohibit both and give all ending/timing rules without volunteering blackmail. Q102 expressly asks the blackmail exception. The existing bare atom must also not be read as an exception for promises/negotiations.','coverage_consequence':'Q102 retains both prohibition and card-text exception; no new question needed.'},
